From 0c53ddbb73b3835e6a54a635745d9dfc39026e6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Joldersma <bennidhamma@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:25:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] [COSMIC] Work around cosmic-comp blur region placement

cosmic-comp positions ext-background-effect-v1 blur regions relative to
the xdg window geometry rather than the surface, and offsets the area it
blurs behind popups by the popup's window geometry offset minus its
toplevel's. With client-side decorations (shadows) this misplaces the
blur. Until cosmic-comp is fixed:

- Shift blur regions to where cosmic-comp expects them, for toplevels
  and popups.
- Keep popups' window geometry offset no larger than their toplevel's,
  so that the blurred area covers them; positioning uses the same
  insets, so popups do not move.

Enabled by WaylandBlurRegionRelativeToWindowGeometry, which defaults to
on when XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP contains COSMIC. Not intended for upstream:
it misplaces the blur on correct compositors, and must be disabled once
cosmic-comp is fixed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
